Step 5: Write Tests for Product Search
Objective: Design and implement comprehensive end-to-end (E2E) tests using Playwright for the product search, filtering, pagination, and sorting features.

Core Prompt:
Create a suite of Playwright E2E tests for the product search experience. The tests must validate user interactions with the search bar, filter controls, pagination, and sort options — covering both happy paths and edge cases.

Test Cases to Implement:
- Search with valid query
- Search with no results
- Apply single filter
- Apply multiple filters
- Clear all filters
- Pagination navigation
- Sort by different criteria

Test Coverage Requirements
1. Search Behavior
    Validate the search bar with both positive and negative scenarios:
        Valid Query
            Enter a keyword that returns results
            Verify matching products are displayed
        No Results
            Enter a query with no matches
            Verify empty state message is shown
        Edge Cases
            Empty string, special characters, whitespace-only input

2. Filter Controls
    Single Filter
        Apply one filter (e.g., category or price range)
        Verify only matching products are shown
    Multiple Filters
        Apply two or more filters simultaneously
        Verify results satisfy all active filters
    Clear All Filters
        Reset all active filters
        Verify full product list is restored

3. Pagination Navigation
    Navigate to the next and previous pages
    Verify correct products are displayed per page
    Verify page state persists on forward/back navigation
    Test boundary pages (first and last)

4. Sort by Different Criteria
    Sort by price (ascending and descending)
    Sort by name (A–Z and Z–A)
    Sort by relevance or rating (if applicable)
    Verify product order changes correctly after each sort selection

Technical Requirements
    Use TypeScript (strict mode, no any)
    Use Playwright Test Runner
    Follow Page Object Model (POM) for maintainability
    Mock network requests where needed (e.g., search and filter API)
    Use data-testid or accessible selectors (avoid brittle selectors)

Expected Output
    Playwright test files:
        /tests/
        ├── search.spec.ts
        ├── filters.spec.ts
        ├── pagination.spec.ts
        └── sort.spec.ts
    Page Object:
        /pages/
        └── SearchPage.ts
    Reusable helpers:
        Query builders
        Filter state utilities